{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>By this you shall know that I am YHWH.</b> The reason He indicated to him knowledge of YHWH through the mediation of this plague is along the lines of what they said, may their memory be for blessing (Exodus Rabbah 9:9), that the Nile was a god to Egypt; therefore YHWH inscribed Himself through the smiting of the river into blood and said, ״By this you shall know that I am YHWH״ — when I execute judgment upon your god. And He was precise in saying <b>I am YHWH</b>, for this name — aside from what they said, may their memory be for blessing (Zohar 3:252a), that it means היה הוה ויהיה ('was, is, and will be') — further intends to say that by His utterance everything comes into being (הַוֶה). And behold, when He strikes His staff upon the river, it will be seen that He, blessed be He, is the one who made the river; He continuously brings it into being at every moment as He desires, and behold, He now brings about in it a different mode of being and turns it into blood." "<b>Further,</b> He hinted to him that from this he would know the measure of His compassion, blessed be He, upon the created beings — seeing before you the river turned to blood, so that you will relent and send them forth and not die. For were it not for the aspect of compassion, He would have struck him and annihilated him from the world — and all the more so by a fortiori: if a great river is turned to blood, an impious sorcerer like him, all the more so. And this is the meaning of His saying <b>by this you shall know that I am YHWH</b> — that I am scheming wisely against you with great matters such as the smiting of your god, so that you may believe and not perish:"], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {0 "The Or HaChaim cites the Zohar's reading of the divine name YHWH as signifying היה הוה ויהיה; I transliterated the key word הווה in parentheses to make visible the wordplay linking 'being' with the name's meaning."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:25:41.169681321Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}